<title>UK: UK region power cut blamed on vandals.</title>
<headline>UK region power cut blamed on vandals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>An explosion at an electricity sub-station which cut off power to more than 26,000 homes and businesses for over an hour on Tuesday night was blamed on vandals, Britain's Press Association news agency reported.</p>
<p>Parts of Cheshire and Staffordshire in northwest England were hit by the cuts, regional supplier Midlands Electricity told the agency.</p>
<p>The Press Association said a spokeswoman blamed &quot;tampering&quot; with the sub-station or with overhead power lines for the explosion and consequent power cuts.</p>
<p>Midlands is owned by Avon Energy, a joint venture between U.S. groups GPU Inc and Cinergy.</p>
